{"status":"completed","summary":"Established a persistent AIDE integrity baseline for `/etc` on node1. AIDE 0.19.2 was installed from signed RHEL repositories, configured to hash every `/etc` entry, initialized, tested with a reversible file modification, and verified clean after restoration and reboot. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were preserved.","actions_performed":["Installed only AIDE and its required nettle dependency.","Added the validated `/etc NORMAL` policy rule.","Created and activated a root-only, SELinux-labeled AIDE database containing 36,014 entries.","Confirmed `aide --check` reports a controlled `/etc/issue` content change, then restored the original file and verified a clean result.","Restarted node1 exactly once and verified changed boot identity, service recovery, baseline persistence, and a clean post-restart check.","Removed test residue and confirmed SELinux remained enforcing, no failed units existed, and listeners remained limited to SSH and loopback chronyd."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Supported software installed without changing the OS release or kernel","command_ids":["cmd-e21f6a7713994458","cmd-c9ff6e93a5314626","cmd-94f93bd0670747f8"],"summary":"Transaction preview and completion show only signed RHEL AIDE 0.19.2 and nettle packages were installed."},{"requirement":"Integrity baseline established for all files under `/etc`","command_ids":["cmd-fdfcf83cb0fd4afa","cmd-149420a58b6e48ba","cmd-575207941aca4c0c","cmd-ccd6428b55cd4b3f"],"summary":"The `/etc NORMAL` rule validated, AIDE initialized 36,014 entries, the protected database was promoted, and the initial check found no differences."},{"requirement":"Later `/etc` changes can be identified and reported","command_ids":["cmd-609a07d3a7744362","cmd-821f41d4decf4e59","cmd-cbf3042b61264005","cmd-6f69332b698c4202"],"summary":"A reversible `/etc/issue` edit was reported as exactly one changed entry with changed size and hashes; restoration returned the check to clean."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-72511f88137d4919","cmd-933d35ac9adf456b","cmd-224c82ae743d4972","cmd-5d46ae8ac1a1446e"],"summary":"Captured healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the safe reboot, proved the boot ID changed, and verified recovered services, unchanged release/kernel, persisted database checksum, and a clean AIDE check."},{"requirement":"Final security, preservation, and cleanup review","command_ids":["cmd-665a19c88ebf40a0","cmd-d73484606b2449d1"],"summary":"Protected configuration checksums match their pre-change values, SELinux is enforcing, no failed units or test residue remain, and final listeners are unchanged."}]}
